All six items are done. Here's a summary of what changed:

**`app/auth.py`** — Implemented `require_api_key`: reads the `X-API-Key` header, rejects missing/invalid keys with HTTP 401, returns the mapped username on success.

**`app/main.py`** — Four changes following existing patterns:

1. **`GET /tasks`** — Added optional query parameters `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` (all combinable, all optional) and `page`/`page_size` (defaults 1 and 20). Filters are applied first, then pagination slices the result.

2. **`POST /tasks`** — Requires auth via `Depends(require_api_key)`. Validates `project_id` exists (404 if not), auto-generates a unique integer ID (`max(existing IDs) + 1`), appends to the in-memory list, returns 201.

3. **`PUT /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Looks up the task by ID, applies only the fields provided in the request body (`exclude_unset=True`), returns 404 if the task doesn't exist.

4. **`DELETE /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Removes and returns the task, returns 404 if not found.

Syntax compilation and route registration both verified — all six endpoint routes are present and correct.
